Why doesn't the model P3.stan require a truncation statement T[1,]?  The poisson_log function gives the raw Poisson PDF - it needs to be deflated by 1 - exp(-lambda) = 1-exp(-exp(alpha)).  Are you making the approximation here that this is equal to 1?  This is valid for moderately sized samples, but not where there are small numbers of counts.

